<Base title="Privacy" description="What Steward and this website do with your data: nothing leaves your computer.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <h2>The app</h2>
  <p>Steward has no accounts and no telemetry. It reads your files, their names and your system's facts on your computer, and sends none of it anywhere. Its index, caches and settings stay in your home folder (<code>~/.cache/steward</code>, <code>~/.local/share/steward</code>).</p>
  <p>Steward connects to the network only when you open a network location, and apt checks for updates the same way it does for every other package.</p>
  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>This site uses no cookies, no analytics and no third-party fonts or scripts. If you switch between light and dark, your choice is stored in your browser only. The server keeps ordinary access logs (address, time, page) for a short time to keep the site running.</p>
  <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
  <p>"Report a Bug" opens the issue tracker in your browser with the Steward version and Ubuntu release filled in. Nothing is sent until you submit the report yourself.</p>
</Base>
